B. Questions the judge or opposing counsel may ask at preliminary hearing or early proceedings (with how to prepare/answer)
Note: preliminary hearings often focus on scheduling, service, and immediate procedural issues. If the matter proceeds to evidentiary hearings/trial, questions will be more substantive.

1. Procedural/service questions
   - Judge: “Have you been properly served?” — Prepare to confirm how and when you were served; bring proof of service or affidavit.
   - Judge: “Do you understand the allegations/complaint?” — Bring a copy of the complaint; ask Amy to summarize key allegations and your position.
   - Opposing counsel: “Did you receive the contract/NDA?” — Have the NDA and related documents ready; know dates you received and returned items.

